WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.520
This closing module brings the OWASP Top 10 back to the HIPAA Security Rule.

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:08.820
In a healthcare application, security defects are not just technical issues;

00:00:09.040 --> 00:00:12.880
they can affect electronic protected health information, patient trust,

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:17.580
clinical workflows, and the evidence an organization relies on during risk management.

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:22.520
Use the OWASP categories as a practical way to discuss where application risk appears.

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:27.700
Broken access control, weak authentication, cryptographic failures, injection,

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:31.360
insecure design, vulnerable components, logging gaps,

00:00:31.580 --> 00:00:36.940
and server-side request forgery can all create paths to unauthorized access, disclosure,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:39.800
alteration, or disruption of ePHI.

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.380
The HIPAA connection is strongest when engineering work is tied to concrete safeguards and

00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:46.640
records.

00:00:46.860 --> 00:00:51.660
Access reviews, server-side authorization checks, encryption decisions,

00:00:51.880 --> 00:00:56.920
secure configuration, dependency management, audit logging, monitoring, incident response,

00:00:57.140 --> 00:01:01.780
and risk analysis should produce evidence that security, privacy, compliance,

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:04.000
and legal stakeholders can review.

00:01:04.220 --> 00:01:08.860
This course is an awareness and planning aid, not a formal compliance determination.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.320
Validate specific safeguard mappings with qualified HIPAA stakeholders,

00:01:13.540 --> 00:01:18.500
document the decisions, and keep improving the application security program as systems,

00:01:18.720 --> 00:01:21.440
threats, and business processes change.
